;\n57\t  Parameters param;\n58\t  PublicKey pk;\n59\t} SharedInfo;\n60\t\n61\t/**\n62\t * @brief Represents an instance of the ACES (Arithmetic Channel Encryption\n63\t * Scheme).\n64\t *\n65\t * This structure represents an instance of the Arithmetic Channel Encryption\n66\t * Scheme (ACES), including shared information and private key components.\n67\t *\n68\t * @param shared_info Shared information for the ACES instance.\n69\t * @param private_key Private key components for the ACES instance.\n70\t */\n71\ttypedef struct {\n72\t  SharedInfo shared_info;\n73\t  PrivateKey private_key;\n74\t} Aces;\n75\t\n76\t/**\n77\t * @brief Represents a ciphertext in the ACES framework.\n78\t *\n79\t * The ACES framework encrypts a message m ∈ ℤₚ as a ciphertext (c,c') according\n80\t * to the following procedure:\n81\t *\n82\t * 1. The first component c is an n-vector over ℤ_q[X]_u given by c = f₀ᵀb,\n83\t * where:\n84\t *    - f₀ is an n × N matrix over ℤ_q[X]_u (chosen during key generation).\n85\t *    - b = (bᵢ)ᵢ is an N-vector over ℤ_q[X]_u such that bᵢ(ω) ∈ {0,1,…,p}\n86\t * (selected by the sender).\n87\t *\n88\t * 2. The second component c' is an element of ℤ_q[X] defined as\n89\t * c' = r_m + cᵀx + e, where:\n90\t *    - r_m is an element over ℤ_q[X]_u chosen such that its evaluation in ℤ_q\n91\t * at the integer ω equals m (chosen by the sender).\n92\t *    - x is an n-vector over ℤ_q[X]_u (considered the private key).\n93\t *    - e is a scalar product in the form of bᵀe', where e' = (eᵢ')ᵢ is an\n94\t * N-vector over ℤ_q[X]_u such that the evaluation of eᵢ' in ℤ_q at the integer\n95\t * ω is equal to a product pℓ where ℓ ∈ {0,1}.\n96\t *\n97\t * @param c1 First component of the ciphertext, represented as a polynomial\n98\t * array.\n99\t * @param c2 Second component of the ciphertext, represented as a polynomial.\n100\t * @param level The level parameter associated with the ciphertext.\n101\t */\n102\ttypedef struct {\n103\t  PolyArray c1;\n104\t  Polynomial c2;\n1